      {
        "id": "comment_main",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# 🎬 Script to Screen\n\nTurns a short brief into a narrated, scored short film, with a storyboard you can check before spending on video.\n\n**How it works:** \"Brief\", \"Visual style\" and \"Shot count\" (5) fill \"Build director brief\", and the Director agent writes the direction document. \"Extract production data\" pulls out narration, a music prompt and a style frame prompt for \"Master style frame\" (FLUX schnell). \"Build shot-list prompt\" drives \"Stream the shots\", which emits one line per shot. Each shot becomes a keyframe in \"Storyboard keyframes (anchored to style frame)\", a Nano Banana edit of the style frame at strength 0.82, collected into the storyboard output. \"Animate each shot (the expensive step)\" makes 4 s Veo 3.1 clips at 720p, joined by \"Cut the shots together\". \"Narration\" (OpenAI tts-1) and \"Score\" (MusicGen, 30 s) are mixed in at volumes 1 and 0.3. Pick language models on the Director agent, \"Extract production data\" and \"Stream the shots\". Media steps need fal, Gemini, OpenAI and Replicate keys.\n\n**Try this:** Bypass \"Animate each shot (the expensive step)\" (right-click, Bypass), set \"Shot count\" to 3, and run to review a cheap three-frame storyboard before any video spend."
        },
        "ui_properties": {
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0
          },
          "zIndex": 0,
          "width": 560,
          "height": 464,
          "selectable": true,
          "bypassed": false
        },
        "dynamic_properties": {},
        "dynamic_outputs": {}
      },
